```ts
export interface RenderBenchmarkOptions {
  /** Simulated frames (default 3600 = 60s @60Hz). */
  frames?: number;
  /** Tuning mode: tuned (default) = merged ships + instanced ore; baseline = legacy. */
  tuned?: boolean;
  monitor?: FrameMonitor;
  wallTimeoutMs?: number;
}

export interface RenderBenchmarkReport {
  tuned: boolean;
  frames: number;
  p50Ms, p95Ms, p99Ms, maxMs: number;
  spikes50Ms: number;
  drawCallsP95, drawCallsMax: number;
  materialsMax: number;
  trianglesMax: number;
  wallMs: number;
  maxLaserFlashes: number;  // observed cap behavior
  maxDebrisSets: number;
  stageMs: { streamer, scene, remotes, fx, ore, labels, tally };
}
```

Scene:
- seed/devSeed fixture (same as transitionCycle): system = generateSystem(seed, starId), planet = system.planets[planetIndex].
- pad = padsForSystem(seed, system)[for that planet]; playerPos = padLocal.
- streamer = new ChunkStreamer(seed, planet); scene = new ChunkScene(streamer, {monitor}); threeScene.
- Background: createBackground(seed, profile.starCount) → sky+stars; scene.add.
- OreRockLayer (instanced: tuned), 30 deposits: deterministic synthetic data around padLocal: for i<30: angle=i/30*2π, r=60+i*12, pos = {x: padLocal.x + cos*r, y: planetHeight? — use planetHeightAt? depositsFor is real… Simpler: use real depositsFor(seed, planet) and take those within 500m of pad? The number is indeterminate. The AC says "30 nearby deposits" — synthesize exactly 30: y = 0 (near pad's padLocal.y), z same; resource cycles through 4 kinds; amount 20.
- combatFx = new CombatFx((scene)=>camera) — attach(scene) returns a camera: `attach: (scene: THREE.Object3D) => THREE.Camera` — the WorldManager passes a function that adds group + returns camera. I'll write `(g) => { threeScene.add(g); return camera; }`.
- fxCaps: tuned → PERF_PROFILES.high.fxCaps; baseline → large caps {laserFlashes: 256, missiles: 16, debrisSets: 16}? Baseline = pre-tuning code had no caps → caps are effectively infinite. Use 9999.
- Remote layer: RemoteEntityLayer; setParent(systemGroup: THREE.Group added to threeScene); setProjector(projector using camera); 16 ships: kind ship (8, with callsign+unique livery) + ai-ship (8, same class). Flight path: circular orbit around player, center at altitude 300, radius 400-500, speed 60 m/s, per-ship phase offset. Feed snapshots every 100ms of simulation time (10Hz), entities move along the path; rot faces the tangent direction (compute quaternion with lookAt direction).
- Hazard disc: buildHazardDiscs(seed, system) → add the group to systemGroup. (8 hazard cells — actual count depends on system; no problem.)
